=======================================================================
DeepSeek Harness (dsh) is installed.
=======================================================================

COMMAND LINE
    dsh --help
    dsh web
    dsh --version

    The launcher is %%PREFIX%%/bin/dsh. The runtime is a pnpm deploy
    tree below %%PREFIX%%/lib/node_modules/deepseek-harness.

WEB UI
    dsh web listens on 127.0.0.1:3080 by default and prints a one-time
    URL containing an access token. Open that URL directly:

        http://127.0.0.1:3080/?token=<token>

    From another machine, forward the port instead of exposing it:

        ssh -L 3080:127.0.0.1:3080 <user>@<host>
        # then open http://localhost:3080/

    The /api browser-trust fence accepts loopback, the listener's own
    bind address, and hosts named by --trusted-host. A reverse proxy on
    a different authority must pass --trusted-host explicitly.

ACCOUNT LOGIN
    DeepSeek account OAuth only accepts a loopback HTTP browser origin.
    Opening the UI as http://10.0.0.3:3080 therefore makes "Sign in"
    fail before the authorization tab opens, even though normal API
    calls are trusted. Use an SSH local forward and open the loopback
    URL instead:

        ssh -N -L 3080:10.0.0.3:3080 <user>@<host>
        # then open http://127.0.0.1:3080/?token=<token>

    An API key configured in Settings, or DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, does not
    have this restriction. Account login is only needed for profile,
    balance and bonus features.

BOOT-TIME SERVICE
    sysrc dsh_web_enable=YES
    service dsh_web start

    The rc script runs as www, keeps state in /var/db/dsh, and prints
    the token URL after startup. Useful overrides:

        sysrc dsh_web_user=someuser
        sysrc dsh_web_chdir=/path/to/state
        sysrc dsh_web_host=127.0.0.1
        sysrc dsh_web_port=3080

    Configuration, sessions and credentials live under DSH_HOME.

SANDBOX
    This port has no FreeBSD sandbox provider. The launcher therefore
    defaults DSH_PERMISSION_MODE to danger-full-access; commands run
    with the invoking user's authority. Set DSH_PERMISSION_MODE to
    another value only after installing a compatible backend.

RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
    node24, bash and ripgrep are installed automatically. The terminal
    tool uses bash for its persistent PTY, and the search tools use the
    system ripgrep rather than a bundled platform binary.

OFFLINE BUILD
    make fetch runs pnpm fetch and stores the dependency cache in an
    extra distfile. Subsequent make build runs without registry access.
    See %%PREFIX%%/share/doc/deepseek-harness/README.FreeBSD.

UPSTREAM
    https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
=======================================================================
